  <data name="Dialog.AlreadyRunning" xml:space="preserve"><value>OverlayUtils is already running: look for its icon near the clock.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.ChooseSwitcher.Filter" xml:space="preserve"><value>MonitorSwitcher|MonitorSwitcher.exe|Programs|*.exe</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.Cancelled" xml:space="preserve"><value>Administrator permission was not given, so nothing was changed.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.CopyFailed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Could not copy OverlayUtils. Details are in errors.log (tray menu → Open settings folder).</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.DisableBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>OverlayUtils will go back to standard mode: it moves to your user folder, removes itself from Program Files and removes the certificate it added.

The overlay will no longer appear over fullscreen games. Windows will ask for administrator permission once.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.DisableIncomplete" xml:space="preserve"><value>OverlayUtils is now in standard mode, but the full-mode copy in Program Files could not be removed. Try again from the tray menu (Overlay over fullscreen games).</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.EnableBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Full mode lets the overlay appear on top of fullscreen games.

Windows allows this only for signed programs installed in Program Files, so OverlayUtils will:
• trust the certificate it is signed with on this PC (only if Windows does not trust it already),
• copy itself to Program Files,
• remove the old AppUtili, if present.

Trusting a certificate means Windows will accept anything signed with it: do this only if you trust whoever gave you OverlayUtils. You can undo everything later from this same menu.

Windows will ask for administrator permission once.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.Failed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Something went wrong. Details are in errors.log (tray menu → Open settings folder).</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.LaunchFailed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Full mode is installed, but Windows refused to start it ({0}). OverlayUtils keeps running in standard mode.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.NotSigned" xml:space="preserve"><value>This copy of OverlayUtils is not signed, so Windows does not allow full mode. Use a signed release, or build one with scripts\build.ps1.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.FullMode.Untrusted" xml:space="preserve"><value>This copy is signed with a certificate that Windows does not trust and that is not a self-signed code-signing certificate. Full mode was not enabled.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.Legacy.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>This removes the old AppUtili: it stops it, deletes it from Program Files, removes its start-up task and the certificate it installed. Your settings have already been copied to OverlayUtils.

Windows will ask for administrator permission once.</value></data>
  <data name="Dialog.Legacy.Done" xml:space="preserve"><value>The old AppUtili has been removed.</value></data>
